   Management; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; German Ind \& Commerce; Off
   European Commiss Hong Kong \& Macao; CSR Asia},
Abstract = {Integrated Water-Energy Management comprises a wide range of solutions
   and methodologies for quite a number of challenges that come along with
   growing scarcity of both drinking water and energy. Traditionally, both
   infrastructure systems - water supply and energy supply - are
   independently organized. Yet, future-oriented solutions that are
   designed to overcome mounting restrictions in water and power supply for
   urban and semi-urban areas, and for industries in particular, ask for
   integrated water-energy management, particularly in developing
   countries. This paper presents three examples which may highlight the
   variety of challenges that have to be addressed.},
