   (2011 ISEST), Dongguan, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 01-04, 2011},
Organization = {Chinese Soc Environm Sci; Beijing Inst Technol; Amer Chem Soc, ENVR Div;
   Beijing Inst Technol, State Key Lab Explos Sci \& Technol; Dongguan Sci
   \& Technol Museum},
Abstract = {Grade of atmospheric environment assessment should be set by the
   estimation model according to ``Guidelines for Environmental Impact
   Assessment-Atmospheric Environment{''} (HJ2.2-2008) in China. For the
   differences in the data processing and diffusion theory between
   prediction model (AERMOD and ADMS) and estimation model(SCREEN3), a
   comparison study of atmospheric prediction is performed by setting
   several scenarios and suggestions are put forward in the end of the
   paper. The results of rural case show that all the maximum concentration
   of the 80-meter intermediate altitude source, 120-meter and 240-meter
   elevated source calculated by SCREEN3 are higher than those by AERMOD
   and ADMS. While for 15-meters low altitude source, the maximum
   concentration calculated by SCREEN3 can't contain those by AERMOD and
   ADMS. The results of urban case show that all the maximum concentration
   of the 120-meter and 240-meter elevated source calculated by SCREEN3 are
   higher than those by AERMOD and ADMS. While for the 15-meters low
   altitude source, the maximum concentration calculated by SCREEN3 can't
   contain those by AERMOD. And the maximum concentration of the 80-meter
   intermediate altitude source calculated by SCREEN3 is less than that of
   ADMS.},
