Organization = {Chalmers Univ Technol},
Abstract = {This study explores the influence of gear-changing behaviour on
   vehicular exhaust emissions and fuel consumption using real drive cycles
   as an input. As many as 235 different drive cycles, recorded from people
   participating in a survey, were imported in an emission simulation tool
   called Vehicle Transient Emissions Simulation Software (VeTESS).
   Emissions and fuel consumption were calculated with VeTESS using two
   different gear change assumptions (normal and aggressive). This paper
   reports on the differences in vehicle exhaust emissions between trips
   made with those two different settings.},
