Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {Energy-saving designs for windows are the most important part in the
   process of thermal-conducting, and decreasing the energy-consumption of
   windows plays an important role during the course of improving the
   indoor thermal-environment and prompting the level of energy-efficiency
   of buildings. It is a great challenge to make energy-consumption design
   in the case of special climate in Hot-Summer and Cold-Winter (HSCW) area
   in China. Taking an existing building for energy efficiency
   reconstruction for example, the article aims at discussing the thoughts
   of how to do the energy saving designs for windows in the HSWC area and
   an analyzed model is made by DOE-plus. According to the simulation
   analysis, many items influenced on the solar radiation and cooling cost
   are analyzed, which included heat insulation of windows, area ration of
   window to wall in different orientations, sun shading and different
   types of window. Finally, though the analysis, some measures are
   discussed to enhance windows' energy-efficiency effect and make some
   helpful reference for the energy-efficiency design and reconstruction of
   windows in HSCW area.},
