   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {The hydro-electrical power station planned to be built at the middle
   reaches of the Yalong River will be a big hydroelectrical construction.
   The area surrounding the planned damsite is complex in engineering
   geological conditions. It has been discovered that there exists a kind
   of extensive and deep-going timedependent deformation-fracture system
   inside the left bank slope. Based on the data of field investigations,
   measurements and simulations (physical and numerical), this paper deals
   with the characteristics, genesis and developing tendency of this
   deformation-fracture system, as well as its possible affection on the
   hydro-electrical construction in future.},
