   Kaifeng, PEOPLES R CHINA, AUG 19-21, 2010},
Organization = {Int Soc Resource Environm Informat Technol},
Abstract = {The water from user-owned wells is an important component of urban water
   supply in Beijing. But in recent years, many problems related to the
   wells have appeared, such as water quality deterioration, water level
   drawdown and reduction of water production capacity. This paper reviewed
   the history of groundwater exploitation by user-owned wells in Beijing
   and analyzed the current situation and the factors affecting user-owned
   wells operation management. Then the water abundance of aquifer was
   selected as the main factor of user-owned wells operation management. To
   improve user-owned wells scientific management, a zoning condition
   evaluation for user-owned wells operation management based on GIS and
   Delphi method was made.},
