Note = {5th International Workshop on Energy and Environment of Residential
   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {Underlying surface condition has significant impact on urban
   microclimate. A field measurement was performed to investigate the
   effects of different underlying surface conditions on surface-air
   temperature distribution in Guangzhou in summer. Infrared thermograph
   and temperature \& humidity data logger were employed to collect the
   surface temperature and near ground (1.5m) air temperature of sunlit
   lawn, sunlit concrete pavement, water body and shady pavement. Maximum
   surface temperatures difference was approximately 25 degrees C, while
   maximum air temperatures difference was 3 degrees C. There was a strong
   correlation between surface temperature and solar radiation intensity.
   The air temperature vertical gradient was high below 0.3m and negligible
   within 0.3m similar to 1.5m. Although the main influence factors of
   horizontal air temperature gradient are underlying surface conditions,
   the influence of wind speed, wind direction and terrain can not be
   neglected. The empirical relationships of land surface temperature and
   air temperature at 1.5m height were developed by linear regression
   analyses for different land surface types.},
