   SLOVAKIA, OCT 24-26, 2002},
Organization = {Int Assoc Landscape Ecol},
Abstract = {The article presents approaches to analysis of visual landscape quality.
   It is based on geographic and landscape-ecological subject of landscape
   research where analysis of visual aspect of the landscape is linked to
   its material entity and human perceptions. The normative approach
   presumes the respect for the physical state of the landscape and applies
   the ecological and aesthetic principles established in advance. It is
   based on identification of the landscape surface objects (land cover and
   relief) and analysis of their horizontal arrangement and vertical
   diversity. Behavioural approach prefers individual perception of man and
   his behaviour. Results of the quoted approaches should be verified by
   mutual combination for further application to the design ecological
   network or assessment of attractiveness of the landscape pattern for the
   purposes of tourism.},
