Abstract = {Over the past 10 years, the rapid urbanization in China has brought
   profound impact on China economy and society, and had certain influence
   on urban micro-climate. Taking Jinan city as an example, based on the
   model about the relation between the urban development and urban climate
   change, the trend of Jinan temperature and precipitation are analyzed,
   the relative impact between the urban climate and the urban development
   is studied. The results show that there are noticeable Heat Island
   Effect and Rain Island Effect in Jinan, the impact on the urban climate
   change caused by the urban development could not precisely match the
   Kuznets Curve in Jinan.},
