   Management Grp; Amer Scholar Press; Jinan Univ, Alumni Assoc},
Abstract = {To explore the mental health of electricity industry employees and its
   influencing factors, questionnaires were used for employees in
   electricity headquarters and its nine branches. The findings were:
   first, the total score and factors scores of electricity industry
   employees' mental health were lower than normal, and the score of
   obsessive-compulsive disorder and depression were higher than other
   factors scores; second, the result of multianalysis showed that the
   electricity industry employees' mental health was affected by social
   support and emotion coping; third, a mediating effect existed between
   social support and mental health, and the mediating variable was emotion
   coping. Thus, the mental health of electricity industry employees had
   its traits compared with other special groups, and less emotion coping
   can compensate for scarce social support and then advance the mental
   health.},
