Abstract = {This article discusses the scientific understanding and the structural
   components of emotional intelligence. Significant contribution to the
   development of this concept did researchers such as P. Selovey, J.
   Meyer, D. Goleman, R. Bar-On, which identified the cognitive and
   personality components. The content of emotional intelligence is
   distinguished understanding of ones emotions and the emotions of others,
   self-motivation, self-control, empathy, flexibility, resistance to
   stress and other personal characteristics that improve efficiency in
   various spheres of life. Relatively new concept in its content focuses
   differentiated assessment of events is the link between reflection
   events and behavior. The end product of emotional intelligence is making
   decisions based on the reflection and understanding of emotions, which
   are differentiated assessment of events. (C) 2013 The Authors. Published
