Note = {5th International Workshop on Energy and Environment of Residential
   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {The application of phase change material in the building envelope is an
   effective method of improving indoor environment comfort and reducing
   energy consumption. This paper studied the thermal performance of the
   concrete wall adding the shape stabilized phase change material. The
   shape stabilized material is composed of paraffin and high-density
   polyethylene. The phase change temperature of the shape stabilized
   material is 27.5 degrees C, and the quality content of paraffin in the
   shape stabilized phase change material is 70\%. Energy-saving effect and
   feasibility of the shape stabilized phase change material wall are
   studied by contrasting with traditional wall. The results showed that
   the surface temperature of the phase change material wall is lower than
   that of traditional wall, and the thermal flow through the phase change
   material wall is smaller than that of traditional wall. The change in
   the temperature and thermal flow of the phase change material wall is
   small. The wall adding the shape stabilized phase change material don't
   occur the leakage in the heating process, so the phase change materials
   are not sealed in the application. Results can provide the basis for the
   application of phase change material wall in the practice building.},
