   Bioscience (ICFEEB), Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 24-25, 2013},
Abstract = {Transgenic plants have been traditionally attacked as non-natural
   products. However, the most modern transgenic varieties are obtained
   using a natural system, based on the interaction between Agrobacterium
   and plants. Agrobacterium integrates fragment of its DNA, called T-DNA,
   into the plant genome. Expression of genes, located in T-DNA leads to
   the development of disease ``crown gall{''} or ``hairy roots{''}.
   Replacing the T-DNA genes on sequences of interest to the people, and
   the transformation of plants by means of such constructs is the basis of
   genetic engineering of plants. However, there are examples of transgenic
   plants obtained by nature. These include some species of Nicotiana.
   Recently, a new example of the plant containing the T-DNA in its genome,
   has been described in our laboratory: TDNA found in Linaria vulgaris and
   Linaria dalmatica. In this paper, we demonstrate, that Linaria acutiloba
   contains T-DNA like sequence. We analyzed sequence of rolC gene of
   Linaria acutiloba and have shown, that it can code full size protein.},
