Note = {3rd International Conference on Hydroinformatics, COPENHAGEN, DENMARK,
   AUG 24-26, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Hydraul Res; Danish Hydraul Inst; UNESCO; Int Org Water
   Quality; Amer Soc Civil Engineers; World Meteorol Org; Danish Acad
   Engineers; Danish Water Resources Comm},
Abstract = {The Wallingford procedure and the simulation models HYDROWORKS and ISIS
   have been used in two recent case studies in Portugal. From 1994 to 1996
   it was carried out the European project SPRINT SP98/2 ``Application of
   Hydraulic Analysis to Sewerage Rehabilitation in Member States{''},
   which main aim was to apply and divulge the Wallingford Procedure for
   rehabilitation of urban drainage systems. The hydrodynamic simulation
   model HYDROWORKS was used to model the Portuguese urban catchment of
   Alcantara, in Lisbon.
   Presently, under the EU Innovation Programme (DGXIII) and the Portuguese
   Specific Program for the Environment 1995, the UPM Procedure is being
   applied to study the impact of the Odivelas drainage system discharges
   into the Povoa River water quality and to point out solutions to improve
   the system behaviour.
   This paper presents a description of the pilot studies, the methodology
   used to set up the models, the results obtained and the main
   difficulties found.},
