   Antalya, TURKEY, APR 22-25, 2010},
Abstract = {As the proportion of older persons in the Islamic Republic of Iran is
   increasing and is expected to be about 10\% of the total population by
   end of the 21st century, health policy makers are seriously concerned
   about what more services to offer the elderly. A qualitative research
   was conducted that aimed at identifying the views of the respondents
   relating to factors that might facilitate or inhibit the process. Seven
   categories were identified; concept of health, lifestyle, spiritual
   belief, personal and family factors, economic and social factors, health
   care services factor, and supportive context. (C) 2010 Elsevier Ltd. All
