   International-Association-for-Engineering-Geology-and-the-Environment,
   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {This paper will presents an automated cartography project using
   CAD/GIS/DBMS technology and Object-Oriented methodology to elaborate the
   Gee-Environmental Database using the Engineering-geological digital map
   of Sao Paulo State, Brazil. The engineering-geological mapping of urban
   and regional areas can be considered as a tool to develop solutions to
   environmental problems. The engineering- geological map should be
   updated due to the modifications of urbanization. The automatic mapping
   can support databases for environmental evaluation of complex and
   accelerated urban dynamics. The automatization of the
   engineering-geological mapping is the objective of a long process, with
   many projects, that has been done since 1992 for the Sao Paulo State, in
   scales 1:10,000, 1:50,000, 1:250,000 to 1:1,000,000. The target of the
   project was to construct: a digital spatial cartographic base; physical
   environmental hazards maps; technological hazards maps; Conservation
   Units spatial data; alpha-numeric data bank; image bank; multimedia; and
   GIS applications.},
