Organization = {Amer Soc Civil Engineers, Environm and Water Resources Inst},
Abstract = {As structures in urban water management have life expectancies up to 100
   years and more, implemented water systems today are strongly influenced
   by historical decisions. In the same way, the current decisions will
   have a long-term impact on the systems. Therefore, it is also important
   to understand the decisions made in the past and its influence on
   today's systems. In this work the historical development of the case
   study Innsbruck is explored over a period of over 100 years. For that,
   all available historic data was collected. Missing data was
   reconstructed and hydraulic Epanet2 models are assembled in 10 year time
   step starting from 1910 up to now. With that data base of network
   models, technical performance over time is analyzed and discussed in
   regard of occurred significant events and their impact on technical
   performance. Further it is outlined, how this information helps in
   addressing current challenges.},
